---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Our Team | Zip Solutions" 
  description="Meet the educators, developers, and accessibility specialists behind Zip Solutions and Zip Captions."
>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="relative bg-gradient-to-b from-white via-alabaster to-slate-100 border-b border-slate-200/80 pt-16 pb-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center">
      <!-- Top Navigation Tabs (Zero Pills) -->
      <div class="inline-flex p-1 bg-slate-200/70 rounded-xl mb-8">
        <a 
          href="/about-us" 
          class="px-5 py-2 rounded-lg text-xs font-bold font-heading bg-white text-midnight shadow-sm"
        >
          Core Team
        </a>
        <a 
          href="/advisory" 
          class="px-5 py-2 rounded-lg text-xs font-bold font-heading text-slate-600 hover:text-midnight transition-colors"
        >
          Advisory Board
        </a>
      </div>

      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amethyst font-heading mb-4">
        Educators • Engineers • Advocates
      </p>

      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-midnight font-heading tracking-tight leading-tight">
        Meet the Team Behind Zip Solutions
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base sm:text-xl text-slate-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        We are a collective of educators and software engineers committed to building a more accessible world. We believe assistive technology should be private, robust, and universally available.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Main Content -->
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14 sm:py-20 space-y-20">

    <!-- Core Values Section -->
    <section>
      <div class="text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-10">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-teal-brand font-heading block mb-1">
          Our Foundation
        </span>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold font-heading text-midnight">
          What Drives Everything We Build
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm space-y-3">
          <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl bg-purple-50 border border-purple-100 flex items-center justify-center text-amethyst">
            <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4.354a4 4 0 110 5.292M15 21H3v-1a6 6 0 0112 0v1zm0 0h6v-1a6 6 0 00-9-5.197M13 7a4 4 0 11-8 0 4 4 0 018 0z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-heading text-midnight">Universal Dignity & Access</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Essential communication tools should never be locked behind steep subscription walls. We ensure our primary live captions remain 100% free forever.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm space-y-3">
          <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl bg-teal-50 border border-teal-100 flex items-center justify-center text-teal-brand">
            <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-heading text-midnight">Strict Privacy by Design</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            No audio recording, no personal telemetry mining, and no selling student or client data. Audio processing happens on your device or via secure, encrypted channels.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm space-y-3">
          <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl bg-slate-100 border border-slate-200 flex items-center justify-center text-midnight">
            <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19.428 15.428a2 2 0 00-1.022-.547l-2.387-.477a6 6 0 00-3.86.517l-.318.158a6 6 0 01-3.86.517L6.05 15.21a2 2 0 00-1.806.547M8 4h8l-1 1v5.172a2 2 0 00.586 1.414l5 5c1.26 1.26.367 3.414-1.415 3.414H4.828c-1.782 0-2.674-2.154-1.414-3.414l5-5A2 2 0 009 10.172V5L8 4z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-heading text-midnight">Classroom & Real-World Proven</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Every feature we design is guided by active educators, certified teachers of the deaf, and people with lived hearing loss experiences.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Team Members Section -->
    <section class="space-y-12">
      <div class="border-b border-slate-200 pb-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold font-heading text-midnight">
          Leadership & Specialists
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 mt-1">
          Passionate professionals bridging educational pedagogy, software architecture, and auditory accessibility.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-8">

        <!-- Member 1: Chris Webb -->
        <article class="bg-white rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm p-6 sm:p-10 lg:p-12 transition-all hover:border-amethyst/40">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 items-start">
            <div class="lg:col-span-4 flex flex-col items-center sm:items-start text-center sm:text-left space-y-4">
              <div class="relative">
                <img 
                  src="/images/Chris_Circle.png" 
                  alt="Chris Webb" 
                  class="w-36 h-36 sm:w-44 sm:h-44 rounded-2xl object-cover border-2 border-purple-100 shadow-md"
                  loading="lazy"
                />
              </div>

              <div>
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold font-heading text-midnight">Chris Webb</h3>
                <p class="text-amethyst font-semibold text-sm font-heading mt-0.5">CEO & Co-Founder</p>
                <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-mono mt-1">Quebec, Canada</p>
              </div>

              <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500 font-mono pt-1">
                Google Certified Innovator • K-13 Computer Science
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-4 text-slate-700 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
              <p>
                Chris is a High School Teacher born in the UK, with rich experience teaching in both the UK and Canada across Kindergarten to Grade 13. With a background in Computer Science, Chris is relentlessly focused on integrating meaningful technology into classrooms and designing practical solutions that empower every student to participate fully.
              </p>
              <p>
                A Google for Education Certified Innovator and Trainer, Chris regularly speaks at educational technology symposiums and conferences. He has presented directly to the Ministry of Education on practical classroom accommodations for students with hearing loss. His articles and insights have been featured across leading publications and was the focus of the Google for Education Global Accessibility Day feature.
              </p>
              <p>
                Chris was the driving inspiration behind Zip Captions through an innovation project with Dell Education Canada. After working closely with members of the d/Deaf community and teaching students who struggled with existing rigid tools, Chris recognized the urgent need for a free, dignified, browser-based live captioning solution. Chris lives in Quebec with his family and three cats.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Member 2: James Petersen -->
        <article class="bg-white rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm p-6 sm:p-10 lg:p-12 transition-all hover:border-teal-200">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 items-start">
            <div class="lg:col-span-4 flex flex-col items-center sm:items-start text-center sm:text-left space-y-4">
              <div class="relative">
                <img 
                  src="/images/James_Circle.png" 
                  alt="James Petersen" 
                  class="w-36 h-36 sm:w-44 sm:h-44 rounded-2xl object-cover border-2 border-teal-100 shadow-md"
                  loading="lazy"
                />
              </div>

              <div>
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold font-heading text-midnight">James Petersen</h3>
                <p class="text-teal-brand font-semibold text-sm font-heading mt-0.5">CTO & Co-Founder</p>
                <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-mono mt-1">Quebec, Canada</p>
              </div>

              <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500 font-mono pt-1">
                Cloud Architect • Open Source Advocate
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-4 text-slate-700 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
              <p>
                James is a full-stack software engineer with over a decade of cloud development expertise. As a former teacher, James brings a unique pedagogical lens to software architecture, passionately believing that technology should empower learners to freely discover, analyze, and use information without friction.
              </p>
              <p>
                James is an unyielding champion of open-source software, decentralized tools, and user privacy, viewing genuine community-building as the true strength of the modern web. He architects the high-performance real-time data pipelines and zero-install browser engines that power Zip Captions, EasySpeak, and our suite of assistive browser extensions.
              </p>
              <p>
                When he isn't shipping updates for Zip Solutions, James spends his free hours tinkering with home automation and IoT hardware—typically involving 3D printing and blinking LEDs. An avid outdoorsman, he enjoys walking his dog through the fields of rural Quebec, canoeing Canada's scenic lakes, and tackling hands-on carpentry projects.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Member 3: Tracey Green -->
        <article class="bg-white rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm p-6 sm:p-10 lg:p-12 transition-all hover:border-amethyst/40">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 items-start">
            <div class="lg:col-span-4 flex flex-col items-center sm:items-start text-center sm:text-left space-y-4">
              <div class="relative">
                <img 
                  src="/images/Tracey_Circle.png" 
                  alt="Tracey Green" 
                  class="w-36 h-36 sm:w-44 sm:h-44 rounded-2xl object-cover border-2 border-purple-100 shadow-md"
                  loading="lazy"
                />
              </div>

              <div>
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold font-heading text-midnight">Tracey Green</h3>
                <p class="text-amethyst font-semibold text-sm font-heading mt-0.5">Accessibility Advisor</p>
                <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-mono mt-1">Ontario, Canada</p>
              </div>

              <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500 font-mono pt-1">
                LSLS Cert AVed • M.A. Child Studies
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-4 text-slate-700 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
              <p>
                Tracey is a certified Teacher of the Deaf (LSLS cert AVed) with extensive experience teaching children with hearing loss to listen, speak, and develop robust self-determination and academic competence in mainstream educational settings.
              </p>
              <p>
                Tracey holds a Master of Arts in Child Studies and Education and has taught in elementary classrooms. She is a Google for Education Certified Teacher and holds distinguished graduate certificates in Auditory-Verbal Studies and Educational Leadership.
              </p>
              <p>
                At Zip Solutions, Tracey provides rigorous pedagogical counsel, ensuring that our AAC tools, speech-to-text displays, and classroom integrations adhere to evidence-based auditory and linguistic accessibility standards.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Advisory Board Teaser Section -->
    <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-900 via-midnight to-slate-950 rounded-3xl p-8 sm:p-12 text-white border border-slate-800 shadow-xl">
      <div class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row items-start lg:items-center justify-between gap-8">
        <div class="space-y-3 max-w-2xl">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-teal-brand font-heading block">
            Guiding Our Vision
          </span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold font-heading">
            Guided by Our Advisory Board
          </h2>
          <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
            Our advisory board brings together certified educators of the deaf, community leaders, and advocates with lived experiences who shape our product roadmap with empathy and rigor.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="shrink-0 w-full sm:w-auto">
          <a 
            href="/advisory" 
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 w-full sm:w-auto px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-heading font-bold text-sm text-midnight bg-white hover:bg-alabaster shadow-lg transition-all"
          >
            <span>Meet the Advisory Board</span>
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M14 5l7 7m0 0l-7 7m7-7H3" />
            </svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
